From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:24:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: play the last sample of a stream segment or loop

voice_get_samples reads while cbo <= ebo (ebo is the last sample), then
moved on when cbo >= ebo: a request that filled up exactly at cbo == ebo
went to the next segment, or back to the loop start, before sample ebo
was played. The resampler asks for ~30 source samples a frame, so about
one seam or loop point in 30 dropped a sample: a click. Same code in
xemu. Now cbo > ebo.

Local change approved by the user (notes 18.49), never pushed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/apu/apu_vp.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/apu/apu_vp.c b/src/apu/apu_vp.c
index 02f7cde..9590124 100644
--- a/src/apu/apu_vp.c
+++ b/src/apu/apu_vp.c
@@ -913,7 +913,13 @@ static int voice_get_samples(MCPXAPUState *d, uint32_t v, float samples[][2],
         }
     }
 
-    if (cbo >= ebo) {
+    /* ebo is the last sample (the loop above runs while cbo <= ebo), so the
+     * segment or buffer is done once cbo has passed it. This was cbo >= ebo,
+     * as in xemu: a request that filled up exactly at cbo == ebo moved on
+     * before sample ebo was played, dropping the last sample of a stream
+     * segment or of a loop about once in 30 (the resampler asks for ~30
+     * source samples a frame), a click each time (notes 18.49). */
+    if (cbo > ebo) {
         if (stream) {
             d->vp.ssl[v].ssl_seg += 1;
             cbo = 0;
